	//*** or we could use this version of the regex that caters for syntax errors
	//*** such as div["id"], div["id"="foo"], div[id=*"foo"], and div[id=foo]
	//*** but it hasn't been tested any more robustly than that it passes those examples
	//*** for eg it might have negative side effects not immediately clear
	//*** check out valid syntax more closely to see which of those are allowed anyway
	//*** and think about what other options there are for dealing with invalid syntax
	//*** such as for exampe, a separate regex for removing invalid ones first and throwing them away
	//REGEX_ATTR_SELECTORS = /(\[\s*[\"\']?\s*[_a-z0-9-:\.\|\\]+\s*[\"\']?\s*(?:[~\|\*\^\$]?\s*[=]?[~\|\*\^\$]?\s*[\"\']?[^\"\']*[\"\']?)?\s*\])/ig,
	
	
